1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,270
This is Parhelion.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:12,170
On Solana, every wallet is public. Join one holder chat, and the whole room can see your balance, your trades, and your next move.

3
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:21,980
Parhelion fixes that. You prove you hold the bag, without ever showing which wallet is yours. The group learns one fact. Nothing else.

4
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:30,150
Here's the app. Connect any Solana wallet, then pick a token and a threshold. Say, a thousand SOL.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,030
Sign once. It's a free message, not a transaction. Parhelion checks your balance on-chain, and issues a proof.

6
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:44,980
Anyone can verify it, with no wallet needed. Valid. And your wallet? Not included.

7
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:51,430
For communities, there's the Telegram bot. An admin gates the group with a single command.

8
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:57,100
When someone asks to join, the bot sends them a link to get their proof.

9
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:04,220
They paste it in, and they're approved automatically. The admins never see a wallet.

10
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:13,340
On Discord, any role becomes a holder role. Members run slash verify with their proof, and get the role instantly.

11
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:20,500
When the proof expires, the role is removed. So your holders are always real.

12
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:27,020
Projects can create a gate in seconds, and share it with their community.

13
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:40,030
Creating a gate costs a small fee in $PRHL. Part of every fee is burned on-chain, in the same transaction.

14
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:50,960
And everything is documented: how it works, the bots, the burn, and the roadmap.

15
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:00,830
Parhelion. Prove you're a whale. Stay invisible.
